WEBVTT

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:02.910
An original cocktail, Boupuet.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:08.840
It was created with the notion in mind that flowers are surrounded by smiles.

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:34.050
Umm...

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.550
Is the bar open yet?

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:41.260
When one arrives
at the bar a little early,

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:46.270
one often pushes the door open
ever so slightly and calls out warily.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:47.980
Then...

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:50.520
when one hears a voice calling,

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:52.400
"Welcome, please come in."

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:56.780
One suddenly feels at ease and
the drinks suddenly taste better.

00:01:58.070 --> 00:01:58.900
However,

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:02.120
if the bar is yet to open,

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:03.950
what must it be like inside...?

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:07.580
A lonely bar counter.

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:10.580
A lonely bar stool.

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:12.130
And...

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:15.590
a brightly lit interior, quite different
from its usual appearance.

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:20.090
Somehow roused by the spirit of adventure,

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:24.010
"I'm not a thief."

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:26.100
"I'm just a customer."

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.100
Telling yourself this
in the back of your mind,

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:33.560
you peer behind the bar, something
you've been dying to do for ages.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:38.150
As you enter the counter you've wanted
to step behind even just once...

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.490
Welcome.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.990
Did he startle you?

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.500
I suppose this is
a slightly embarrassing situation...

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:53.420
But then, why not just pull up a pew.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.300
Let us prepare you a slightly unusual
cocktail, as an apology for startling you.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:06.310
Is something the matter?

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.520
Do you dislike thunder?

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:09.350
Huh?

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:10.730
Er, well.. I guess...

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:14.770
Actually, I was wondering if
you might be closed today.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:16.110
No.

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:20.070
I was just thinking of opening
the bar a little later than usual.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:21.280
Later than usual?

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:22.360
Yes.

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:24.910
I thought up a new cocktail.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:29.200
So I was waiting for my seniors
to arrive so they could taste it.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.750
In that case,
I'll come back some other time.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:33.000
It's fine, don't worry.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.330
There's thunder.

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:36.420
That means the rain will come soon.

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:45.970
See, just as I said.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:47.970
PIease wait a moment.

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:54.270
What's the matter?

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:56.310
Oh, nothing...

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:57.400
Now then.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.190
What cocktail would you
like me to prepare you?

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:02.570
-Erm, yes, well...
-No...

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:05.410
Actually, I think I've guessed...

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:14.170
Here, enjoy.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:16.710
A Black Witch.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:23.130
You used dry ice just now, right?

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.890
Huh? Did I put something in it?

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.760
Would you try it for me first?

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:33.520
I'm sorry, miss. A bartender is
no more than a "gentle perch".

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:35.640
What's that supposed to mean...?

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:38.520
I can't. This drink has
something weird about it.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.230
I'm going home.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:42.740
PIease hold on.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.450
Did I say something to offend?

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:58.170
Are... are you okay?

00:04:58.710 --> 00:04:59.840
What a fever!

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:01.840
What to do? What to do?

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:04.720
I know!

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:06.430
I have to get someone.

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:11.100
Is there a doctor?

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:15.980
Erm... I'm pretty sure it's nearby...

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:19.860
Piece of shit map...

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:23.110
Taxi! Wait!

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:33.830
What're you doing, you piece of shit?

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:36.540
I'm sorry! I'm in a rush!

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:42.210
What the hell?

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:43.920
Huh?

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:45.670
My map...

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:47.550
PIease hurry, driver!

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:48.840
Certainly...

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:54.430
Must be a blackout.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:55.850
No one's here.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:58.270
What in the name of...?

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:00.900
Good job we know our way around Eden hall.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:03.690
-Oops!
-Watch your step.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:06.150
I've found the fuse box.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:08.860
Now then.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.570
The lights are on but...

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:16.080
I don't mind being called out
to try a new cocktail but... Oh!

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:24.960
Mr Higashiyama. Mr Kuzuhara.

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:30.510
Here, just rest.

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:34.810
Well, we can't just go home now.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:38.730
We need to give the patient something
that's good for his ailment.

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:40.140
I'll get on it.

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:42.190
Oh, no, wait. I'll go fix him something.

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:44.570
What're you talking about,
I'm puite able to.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:47.570
I said I would first, though...

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:50.780
-No you didn't, I did...
-But you didn't, I did...

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:55.950
Well, how about we both prepare
something for the lad? Starting with me.

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:58.870
Very well. We can go by seniority, then.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:04.170
Now, I will take leave momentarily.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:10.970
What should I do?
We have four or five cars tailing us.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:13.930
I don't care. We'll follow the plan.

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:20.680
I'm sorry.

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:22.480
We're closed this evening.

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:23.440
Like hell you are!

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:26.190
We've got an appointment here tonight.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:32.200
Excuse me, we saw someone that looked like
the politician Kouji Souma walk in here!

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:35.240
-Is he holding a secret meeting?
-Is there anyone else in here?

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:36.990
May we come inside your bar?

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:40.910
I'm afraid we're closed this evening.

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:42.290
Now, if you'll excuse us.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:44.630
-PIease open the door.
-PIease!

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:46.960
What's going on?

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:49.550
You're not going to
kick me out on your day off?

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:50.590
No.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.630
You're in our bar now,
so you're a customer.

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:56.180
I believe the owner
would say the same thing.

00:07:56.930 --> 00:08:01.180
Truth of the matter is I'd heard I might
be able to enjoy a Glass of the Gods here.

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:06.270
I thought I'd have that as my last drink
so I chose this as the meeting place.

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:07.860
Unfortunately...

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:10.030
the owner is currently indisposed.

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:13.740
Well, give me whatever then.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:15.700
I hope I will do.

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:18.410
An OId Parr.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:23.460
I wasn't expecting you to know
the politician's favourite drink.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:29.670
Do you know...?

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:33.130
Why the OId Parr is
a favourite among politicians?

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.140
In 1377,

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:39.850
Imperial Minister Tomomi Iwakura, brought
it back following his diplomatic mission.

00:08:39.970 --> 00:08:44.980
Since then, it's been loved by Japan's top
politicians starting with Shigeru Yoshida.

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:50.400
You could almost say
this drink is like a symbol to us.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:52.110
That is not all.

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:53.030
What?

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:00.490
Even if cornered and about to fall,
it stands its ground.

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:05.160
They say that politicians
come to seek this even at the end.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:11.880
Excellent!

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:14.130
You're telling me
all that's left for me now

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:16.340
is no more than the sight of this bottle.

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:22.390
To think I became a politician for
something like this. What a joke!

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:25.890
And to top it off, this is how it ends?

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:27.770
If I knew it would end this way,

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:32.070
I would have been honest and walked
a path that aligned with my dreams.

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:36.030
<i>What makes the desert heautiful...</i>

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:38.860
<i>is that somewhere it hides a well.</i>

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:41.530
<i>What is heautiful,</i>

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:44.080
<i>what is essential is invisible to the eye.</i>

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:47.210
"The Little Prince", unless I'm mistaken.

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:48.370
That's right.

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:51.420
You might not believe it,
but I was a literature student.

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:54.840
At one point I even thought of
becoming a children's author.

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:58.260
But because I'd come from
a long line of politicians.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:00.260
My dad told me...

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:04.470
"You'll have time to dream
when you're sleeping."

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:08.520
That's why I've worked all my life

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:12.610
believing there was something invisible
but essential in the world of politics.

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:15.610
And here, in front of you, is the result.

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:19.950
I wonder what kind of customer
I look like now.

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:22.200
A somewhat tired one.

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:24.490
One who has Iost confidence.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:26.870
I see...

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:31.040
In that case,
give me something you think is befitting.

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:33.500
I've got to get going soon.

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:34.880
In that case...

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:40.840
Five parts of OId Parr,
one part Drambuie and stir.

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:44.260
Drambuie?

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:46.600
It's an old drink from Scotland.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:51.730
A sweet liqueur that combines honey and
certain herbs with a Scotch whisky base.

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:55.020
In Gaelic, its name means
"the drink that satisfies".

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:58.780
The great actor, Humphrey Bogart,
was very fond of this drink.

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:06.450
I see. A profound flavour
that has dignity.

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:10.160
The hint of sweetness and
whisky aroma harmonise

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:12.330
as it spreads with complexity
across the palate.

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:15.130
It is called a Rusty Nail.

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:18.090
Rusty Nail?

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:20.590
A nail that has rusted...?

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:25.350
Are you poking fun at me, suggesting
I brought all this on myself?

00:11:25.430 --> 00:11:26.180
Oh, no, sir.

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:30.140
A rusted nail can shine once again,
with a little polish.

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:33.230
Bars are there to polish weary
customers' rusty hearts,

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:36.060
with spirits,
to make them shine once again.

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:38.860
Make them shine again, with spirits...?

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:42.490
Even if a customer has
the whole world against him,

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:46.910
the bartender must remain his final ally.

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:48.540
The last drink

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:51.960
that can save a soul wounded by
loneliness, with nowhere left to go.

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:53.960
The Glass of the Gods.

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:56.170
We bartenders

00:11:56.790 --> 00:12:00.590
wait anxiously to serve such a drink.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:04.180
So that is the well
in the desert you spoke of?

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:05.760
Is it?

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:14.850
The Glass of the Gods, eh...

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:18.020
Out of the way, you paparazzi parasites!

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:21.280
A politician's righteousness is judged
100 years down the Iine!

00:12:21.610 --> 00:12:24.450
I, Kouji Souma, will neither run nor hide.

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:29.200
Now, I'm going to the Public Prosecutor's
Office to prove my innocence!

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:39.000
What was all the commotion about?

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:41.510
Huh...? Did a customer come in?

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:44.340
No... Just someone
taking shelter from the rain.

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:47.550
Have you finished, Mr Kuzuhara?

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:50.310
No. I'm still mid-preparation.

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:52.350
In that case, I shall prepare mine.

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:53.850
We can swap places.

00:12:56.600 --> 00:12:57.770
I found it at last.

00:12:58.190 --> 00:13:01.940
It's that blasted woman's fault
I lost my map, and now look at me!

00:13:02.730 --> 00:13:05.280
Hey. Can't you see I'm soaked through?

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:06.950
Get me a towel, would you?

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:08.320
Certainly, miss.

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:18.250
Say. I've got a rendezvous here.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:19.920
Did anybody come in?

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:20.790
Well...

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:25.720
Actually, the bar is closed, today.
As you can see, the owner's unwell...

00:13:27.220 --> 00:13:28.840
That damn piece of shit!

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:30.220
Piece of shit...?

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:31.180
Damn right!

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:33.850
It was the client
who repuested we meet here!

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:37.390
Even if I am a bit late,
he could have waited!

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:40.770
And now, because he suggested this place,
the whole thing's going down the drain!

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:42.860
I was gonna get
a good job out of this, too!

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:53.490
Seriously though...

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:57.750
Why do I always have to deal with
such complete pieces of shit?

00:13:58.290 --> 00:14:00.380
All they have to do is
leave it with me, but no...

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:02.170
They don't even show up!

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:05.880
I even turned down another job
and took ages getting ready.

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:07.880
Piece of shit.

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:09.430
Are you even listening?

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:12.850
I am. What a real piece of shit.

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:14.310
Whatever...

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:16.850
Just gimme a drink
while I hide from the rain.

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:17.810
In that case.

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:22.310
Hang on. As I'm here, how about making me
a cocktail I haven't tried before?

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:25.110
A cocktail you haven't tried before?

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:26.570
Right.

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:28.240
A Glass of the Gods!

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:30.200
A Glass of the Gods?

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:32.200
What kind of cocktail
would that be for me?

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:36.330
Well... that depends on the customer.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:38.660
The client I was meant to meet
told me about it.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:40.540
One Glass of the Gods.

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:41.880
Listen here.

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:44.800
The customer has the right
to make outlandish requests.

00:14:45.590 --> 00:14:47.630
That's what we pay you money for.

00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:51.970
Anyway, the Glass of the Gods will be
a cocktail I've never had before, right?

00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:56.140
So I want you to make me a drink
other than those I'm about to list.

00:14:56.520 --> 00:14:57.220
Ready?

00:14:57.390 --> 00:15:00.440
Earthquake, AIaska, Emerald, Angel's Tip.

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:03.060
Campari, Kir, Gibson, Cuba Libre,

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:06.110
Green Eyes, Copenhagen,
Side Car, Jack Rose,

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:09.320
-Shanghai, Daipuiri, Dog's Nose.
-Bull Shot.

00:15:09.650 --> 00:15:10.610
Huh?

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:12.070
Bull Shot.

00:15:12.610 --> 00:15:14.200
What's that?

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:16.330
Like I said. Bull Shot.

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:19.660
Okay then. I've never heard of it.

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:30.880
Sorry to keep you.

00:15:31.170 --> 00:15:32.220
Your Bull Shot.

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:36.850
I would very much like you
to give this a try.

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:39.770
Seriously?
This looks Iike regular soup.

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:47.440
What? There's some
kind of alcohol in here.

00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:50.570
Quite. We start with beef bouillon.

00:15:51.070 --> 00:15:54.070
You can use a stock cube if you wish,

00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:57.490
but you need 90 ml warmed
and poured into the cup.

00:15:57.870 --> 00:16:00.620
Next we add 45 ml or so of vodka.

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:04.330
Then a little Worcester sauce and
pepper, if one wishes.

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:07.500
It came about in the 1950s,

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:10.880
and is said to have been created by
an American steak house owner,

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:14.090
the Caucus Club's Les Gruber.

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:17.640
It's delicious.

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:20.310
Who knew such a cocktail existed?

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:23.390
I feel my rain-drenched bones

00:16:23.770 --> 00:16:26.650
being warmed by the broth
as though I am coming back to life.

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:30.820
I'm sorry about earlier.

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:33.860
You must've have thought
"Where'd this one come from?"

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:36.990
But you can't say that
in your line of work.

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:42.540
Being a bartender is a piece of shit job
for people who can take non-stop bitching.

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:43.290
Hm.

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:45.250
We're the same there.

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:48.840
I mean... Most of the jobs
that come my way involve

00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:52.090
wiping the arses of self-absorbed people
who deserve what they get.

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:53.720
But you know what?

00:16:54.170 --> 00:16:55.720
If today's job were to go to plan,

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:59.510
my trustworthiness would soar and
I might realise my dream of going solo.

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:01.060
Or that's what I'd hoped.

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:07.810
Miss, have you heard the expression,
"one for the road"?

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:09.480
I have not.

00:17:09.810 --> 00:17:14.780
The dictionary defines it as meaning,
"a drink meant to delay parting".

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:18.280
Now, with whom are
you delaying a parting?

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:23.660
Our everyday lives are not filled with
only good things.

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:28.120
And it is the way of the adult world to
misrepresent and deceive oneself at times.

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:31.800
And so "for the road",
implies "for the road home".

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:33.800
And "one" means...

00:17:34.090 --> 00:17:35.130
One glass.

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:41.220
Perhaps, the one we really say goodbye to
with a drink at the bar is our unpleasant,

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:44.180
piece of shit self.

00:17:45.180 --> 00:17:49.730
I say goodbye to my unpleasant self and
change my mood with this one drink.

00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:01.240
Is it against the rules to have
"one more for the road"?

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:04.370
That sounds perfectly acceptable.

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:09.540
Now, how about adding some lemon juice,
tomato juice to your bull shot,

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:11.790
and trying what's known
as a "BIoody Bull"?

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:26.600
Sorry you had to put up with
a customer Iike me on your day off.

00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:27.390
Not at all, miss.

00:18:27.930 --> 00:18:29.640
It may just be coincidence,

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:33.520
but I take pleasure in my work, just the
same as the customer does in hers,

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:36.940
even as she may come to the bar
in need of a pick-me-up.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:43.740
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:48.960
Bull Shot. Bull Shot.

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:52.580
What's this?

00:18:53.290 --> 00:18:55.420
Mystery novel, Bullshot

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:57.590
Author, Gabriele Kraft.

00:18:57.670 --> 00:19:00.880
The protagonist is a scary-looking lawyer,
who always says "piece of shit",

00:19:01.050 --> 00:19:04.680
but who, in actual fact,
is very kind-hearted.

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:11.350
I take pleasure in my work, just the
same as the customer does in hers.

00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:16.020
The bartender knew what my job was.

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:22.030
Yes? Yes.

00:19:22.360 --> 00:19:25.120
What? Kouji Souma is
seeking representation?

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:29.580
You serious? He's going to fight them?

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:30.960
Got it!

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:32.960
We're changing direction!

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:34.920
To the Tokyo Public Prosecutor's Office!

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:37.800
I'm coming for you!

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:42.220
I see. A bag, you say?

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:43.130
Yes.

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:47.060
It's big and strong enough to carry
Iots of documents.

00:19:47.260 --> 00:19:52.230
A "lawyer's bag" that was famously used by
the American Secretary of State.

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:54.690
A solicitor's briefcase, effectively...

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:57.360
Impressive as always, Mr Kuzuhara.

00:19:58.020 --> 00:19:59.780
I've learned a lot from your example.

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:01.400
What are you talking about?

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:06.910
Your Rusty Nail pierced right
through my heart, you know.

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:09.660
-Ha. That was a good one.
-Not at all.

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:12.250
Honestly!

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:15.250
No doctor would come here!

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:17.380
So I brought some medicine with me.

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:19.380
Oh, well, well.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:21.970
We'll Ieave the rest to you in that case.

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:23.970
-Okay.
-Ah, yes...

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:26.470
I made something healthy for him to drink.

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:30.720
Heat some up and make him
drink it when he wakes up.

00:20:31.220 --> 00:20:34.940
Regrettably, I had to serve mine to a
customer so I chose a good bottle instead.

00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:38.190
Make sure he drinks some.

00:20:38.310 --> 00:20:39.480
Okay...

00:20:45.860 --> 00:20:48.910
Even if the bar happens to be closed,

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:52.000
if a customer should turn up,

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:55.620
there is always a glass
suited to that encounter.

00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:57.710
However,

00:20:58.420 --> 00:21:01.130
for tonight at least, please be quiet.

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:13.770
RECIPE: SCOTCH WHISKY - 40ml
DRAMBUIE - 20mI

00:22:28.170 --> 00:22:30.890
Project supervisor: Justine Cocquyt
Spotting: EIouan Tapounie

00:22:35.640 --> 00:22:38.560
